#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:4
msgid "BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の強誘電不安定性の起源"
msgstr "Origin of the Ferroelectric Instability of BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:6
msgid ""
"立方晶のBaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ では、\\ :ref:`極性ソフトモード<polar-soft-mode>`\\ が0 "
"Kの計算で\\ :ref:`虚数振動数<imaginary-frequency>`\\ "
"をもち、Tiと酸素が逆向きにずれた構造のほうがエネルギーが低い。本稿では、この不安定性がどの相互作用の釣り合いから "
"生じるかを、長距離のクーロン相互作用、短距離の反発、Ti 3d–O 2pの混成の三つに分けて説明する。続いて、これらの相互作用を "
"取り込んだ有限温度の計算が、相の順序と転移の性格について示したことをまとめる。4つの相の構造と分域は「\\ "
":ref:`ferroelectricity`\\ 」、 分極の大きさの求め方は「\\ :ref:`periodic-"
"polarization`\\ 」で扱う。"
msgstr ""
"In cubic BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , the \\ :ref:`polar soft mode <polar-soft-"
"mode>` \\ has an \\ :ref:`imaginary frequency <imaginary-frequency>` \\ "
"in calculations at 0 K, and the structure in which Ti and oxygen shift in"
" opposite directions is lower in energy. This article explains the "
"balance behind the instability in terms of three contributions: long-"
"range Coulomb interactions, short-range repulsion, and Ti 3d–O 2p "
"hybridization. It then summarizes what finite-temperature calculations "
"that include these interactions reveal about the phase sequence and the "
"character of the transitions. For the structures and domains of the four "
"phases, see \\ :ref:`Ferroelectricity and Crystal Structure "
"<ferroelectricity>`\\ . For how to calculate the magnitude of the "
"polarization, see \\ :ref:`Polarization in Periodic Crystals <periodic-"
"polarization>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:11
msgid ""
"**前提知識**: :ref:`BaTiO₃の4つの相<batio3-four-phases>`、:ref:`秩序変数としてのモードの振幅<sm-"
"landau>`、:ref:`立方晶BaTiO₃の不安定なΓ点モード<phonon-batio3-example>`、:ref:`Born有効電荷"
"<fo-born-charge>`、:ref:`軌道の混成とスペクトルの重なり<orbital-"
"hybridization>`、:ref:`Löwdin解析<lowdin>`。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: :ref:`The four phases of BaTiO₃ <batio3-four-phases>`,"
" :ref:`mode amplitude as an order parameter <sm-landau>`, :ref:`the "
"unstable Γ-point mode in cubic BaTiO₃ <phonon-batio3-example>`, "
":ref:`Born effective charges <fo-born-charge>`, :ref:`orbital "
"hybridization and spectral overlap <orbital-hybridization>`, and "
":ref:`Löwdin analysis <lowdin>`."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:13
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:15
msgid "ソフトモードの復元力を、短距離の反発と長距離のクーロン相互作用の和として説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Explain the restoring force of the soft mode as the sum of short-range "
"repulsion and long-range Coulomb interactions."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:16
msgid "双極子どうしの相互作用の角度依存から、Tiの変位が鎖状にそろいやすい理由を導く。"
msgstr ""
"Use the angular dependence of dipole–dipole interactions to derive why Ti"
" displacements tend to align in chains."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:17
msgid "Ti 3d–O 2pの混成が不安定性に必要であることを示した計算と、PDOSだけでは言えないことを区別する。"
msgstr ""
"Distinguish the evidence from calculations that establish the need for Ti"
" 3d–O 2p hybridization from the more limited conclusions available from "
"the PDOS alone."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:18
msgid "第一原理の有効ハミルトニアンによる有限温度の計算が、相の順序と、変位型・秩序–無秩序型の判定について示したことを説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Explain what finite-temperature calculations with a first-principles "
"effective Hamiltonian show about the phase sequence and whether the "
"transition is displacive or order–disorder."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:23
msgid "長距離のクーロン相互作用と短距離の反発"
msgstr "Long-Range Coulomb Interactions and Short-Range Repulsion"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:25
msgid ""
"極性ソフトモードの振幅を :math:`Q` とすると、高温相のまわりのエネルギーは :eq:`sm-landau` の "
":math:`E(Q)=E_0+\\frac12\\kappa Q^2+\\cdots` で表され、:math:`\\kappa<0` "
"なら立方晶は不安定である。 この曲率を、起源の異なる二つの寄与に分けて"
msgstr ""
"Let :math:`Q` be the polar soft-mode amplitude. From Equation :eq:`sm-"
"landau`, the energy around the high-temperature phase is "
":math:`E(Q)=E_0+\\frac12\\kappa Q^2+\\cdots`, and the cubic structure is "
"unstable if :math:`\\kappa<0`. Split the curvature into two contributions"
" with different origins:"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:29
msgid ""
"\\kappa=\\kappa_{\\mathrm{SR}}+\\kappa_{\\mathrm{C}},\\qquad "
"\\kappa_{\\mathrm{SR}}>0,\\quad \\kappa_{\\mathrm{C}}<0"
msgstr ""
"\\kappa=\\kappa_{\\mathrm{SR}}+\\kappa_{\\mathrm{C}},\\qquad "
"\\kappa_{\\mathrm{SR}}>0,\\quad \\kappa_{\\mathrm{C}}<0"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:34
msgid ""
"と書く。:math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm{SR}}` "
"は、変位で近づいた原子どうしの電子雲が重なることによる短距離の反発で、立方晶を安定にする。 "
":math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm{C}}` は、変位で生じた電気双極子どうしの長距離のクーロン相互作用で、極性の変位を促す。 "
"強誘電性はこの二つの釣り合いで決まり、\\ :math:`|\\kappa_{\\mathrm "
"C}|>\\kappa_{\\mathrm{SR}}` のとき不安定になる [PdosCohen1992]_。 "
"第一原理計算の力定数をこの二つに分ける方法には任意性があるが、物質ごとの傾向を理解するのに使われている [Ghosez1999]_。"
msgstr ""
"The contribution :math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm{SR}}` is short-range repulsion,"
" which stabilizes the cubic structure and arises when displacement brings"
" atoms close enough for their electron clouds to overlap. The "
"contribution :math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm{C}}` is the long-range Coulomb "
"interaction between electric dipoles created by displacements and favors "
"polar displacements. Ferroelectricity depends on the balance between the "
"two. The structure becomes unstable when \\ :math:`|\\kappa_{\\mathrm "
"C}|>\\kappa_{\\mathrm{SR}}` [PdosCohen1992]_. Although the decomposition "
"of first-principles force constants into these two contributions is not "
"unique, it is used to understand trends across materials [Ghosez1999]_."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:39
msgid ""
"クーロン相互作用の寄与の形は、双極子どうしの相互作用から分かる。単位胞 :math:`i` の局所的なモードの振幅を "
":math:`\\boldsymbol u_i`、モードの有効電荷（各原子の\\ :ref:`Born有効電荷<fo-born-"
"charge>`\\ をモードの変位の比で重み付けて足したもの）を :math:`Z^*` とすると、胞 :math:`i` の双極子は "
":math:`\\boldsymbol d_i=Z^*e\\,\\boldsymbol u_i` "
"である。Zhongらの有効ハミルトニアンでは、双極子どうしのエネルギーを"
msgstr ""
"The form of the Coulomb contribution follows from dipole–dipole "
"interactions. Let the local mode amplitude in unit cell :math:`i` be "
":math:`\\boldsymbol u_i`, and let the mode effective charge (the sum of "
"the atomic \\ :ref:`Born effective charges <fo-born-charge>` \\ weighted "
"by the relative displacements of the mode) be :math:`Z^*`. The dipole in "
"cell :math:`i` is :math:`\\boldsymbol d_i=Z^*e\\,\\boldsymbol u_i`. Write"
" the dipole–dipole interaction energy as"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:42
msgid ""
"E_{\\mathrm{dpl}}=\\frac{(Z^*e)^2}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0\\varepsilon_\\infty}\\sum_{i<j}"
"\n"
"\\frac{\\boldsymbol u_i\\cdot\\boldsymbol u_j-3(\\hat{\\boldsymbol "
"R}_{ij}\\cdot\\boldsymbol u_i)(\\hat{\\boldsymbol "
"R}_{ij}\\cdot\\boldsymbol u_j)}{R_{ij}^3}"
msgstr ""
"E_{\\mathrm{dpl}}=\\frac{(Z^*e)^2}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0\\varepsilon_\\infty}\\sum_{i<j}"
"\n"
"\\frac{\\boldsymbol u_i\\cdot\\boldsymbol u_j-3(\\hat{\\boldsymbol "
"R}_{ij}\\cdot\\boldsymbol u_i)(\\hat{\\boldsymbol "
"R}_{ij}\\cdot\\boldsymbol u_j)}{R_{ij}^3}"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:48
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"とする [Zhong1995]_。:math:`\\boldsymbol R_{ij}` は胞 :math:`i` から :math:`j` "
"へのベクトル、:math:`\\varepsilon_\\infty` は電子の分極による 遮蔽を表す高周波の誘電率である。同じ向きの2つの変位 "
":math:`\\boldsymbol u_i=\\boldsymbol u_j=\\boldsymbol u` について、 "
":math:`\\boldsymbol R_{ij}\\parallel\\boldsymbol u`\\ （縦に並ぶ）なら分子は "
":math:`u^2-3u^2=-2u^2` でエネルギーが下がり、 :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"R_{ij}\\perp\\boldsymbol u`\\ （横に並ぶ）なら :math:`+u^2` "
"で上がる。双極子は変位の方向に沿って縦に並ぶとき 互いを安定にするので、Tiの変位はTi–O–Tiの鎖に沿ってそろいやすい。立方晶の\\ "
":ref:`フォノン分散<phonon-batio3-example>`\\ で、 "
"不安定な分枝がΓ点からXとMの方向へ平らに広がるのは、この鎖状の相関の表れである。:eq:`fo-dipole` の係数は "
":math:`(Z^*)^2/\\varepsilon_\\infty` に比例するので、有効電荷が大きいほど "
":math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm C}` の不安定化が強くなる。"
msgstr ""
"This is the form used in the effective Hamiltonian of Zhong and coauthors"
" [Zhong1995]_. Here :math:`\\boldsymbol R_{ij}` is the vector from cell "
":math:`i` to cell :math:`j`, and :math:`\\varepsilon_\\infty` is the "
"high-frequency permittivity, which accounts for screening by electronic "
"polarization. For two equal displacements :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"u_i=\\boldsymbol u_j=\\boldsymbol u`, if :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"R_{ij}\\parallel\\boldsymbol u` \\ (end to end), the numerator is "
":math:`u^2-3u^2=-2u^2` and the energy decreases. If :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"R_{ij}\\perp\\boldsymbol u` \\ (side by side), it is :math:`+u^2` and the"
" energy increases. Dipoles stabilize each other when lined up end to end "
"along the displacement direction, so Ti displacements tend to align along"
" Ti–O–Ti chains. In the \\ :ref:`phonon dispersion <phonon-"
"batio3-example>` \\ of the cubic phase, the unstable branch is flat from "
"the Γ point toward X and M, reflecting these chain-like correlations. The"
" coefficient in Equation :eq:`fo-dipole` is proportional to "
":math:`(Z^*)^2/\\varepsilon_\\infty`, so a larger effective charge "
"strengthens the destabilizing effect of :math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm C}`."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:56
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Ghosezらは、立方晶BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の原子間力定数をこの二つに分けて調べた "
"[Ghosez1999]_。1つの原子だけを動かしたときに "
"その原子に働く復元力の係数（自己力定数）は全ての原子で正で、孤立した変位はどれも安定である。不安定性は、複数の原子が協調して動くときだけ生じる。原子間の力定数は、ある原子の変位で別の原子に働く力の係数で、負の値は相手を同じ向きへ引く結合を表す。Tiの自己力定数"
" :math:`+0.1522\\ \\mathrm{Ha/Bohr^2}` に対し、変位の方向に並ぶ隣のTiとの力定数は1本あたり "
":math:`-0.0672\\ \\mathrm{Ha/Bohr^2}` "
"で、鎖の両隣の2本で自己力定数の約9割を打ち消す。横に並ぶTiとの力定数は :math:`+0.0075\\ "
"\\mathrm{Ha/Bohr^2}` と小さい。Tiと鎖の上の酸素の間の力定数では、双極子の寄与 :math:`+0.2325` "
"と短距離の寄与 :math:`-0.2231` が逆符号でほぼ打ち消し合い、和は :math:`+0.0094\\ "
"\\mathrm{Ha/Bohr^2}` にすぎない。大きな二つの寄与のわずかな差で 符号が決まることが、:eq:`fo-kappa-split`"
" の釣り合いの数値上の姿である。"
msgstr ""
"Ghosez and coauthors split the interatomic force constants of cubic "
"BaTiO\\ :sub:`3` \\ into these two contributions [Ghosez1999]_. The "
"restoring force coefficient for an atom displaced on its own (the on-site"
" force constant) is positive for every atom, so all isolated "
"displacements are stable. The instability arises only when several atoms "
"move together. An interatomic force constant relates the force on one "
"atom to the displacement of another. A negative value indicates a "
"coupling that pulls the second atom in the direction of the first atom's "
"displacement. The Ti on-site force constant is :math:`+0.1522\\ "
"\\mathrm{Ha/Bohr^2}`. The force constant with each neighboring Ti along "
"the displacement direction is :math:`-0.0672\\ \\mathrm{Ha/Bohr^2}`, so "
"the two neighbors along the chain cancel about 90% of the on-site "
"constant. The force constant with a Ti beside the chain is small, "
":math:`+0.0075\\ \\mathrm{Ha/Bohr^2}`. For Ti and oxygen along the chain,"
" the dipolar contribution :math:`+0.2325` and short-range contribution "
":math:`-0.2231` have opposite signs and nearly cancel, leaving a sum of "
"only :math:`+0.0094\\ \\mathrm{Ha/Bohr^2}`. The small difference between "
"two large contributions determines the sign, illustrating the balance in "
"Equation :eq:`fo-kappa-split` numerically."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:63
msgid "局所電場の考え方でBaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の不安定性を説明する試みは、Slaterにさかのぼる [Slater1950]_。"
msgstr ""
"Attempts to explain the instability of BaTiO\\ :sub:`3` \\ in terms of "
"local electric fields go back to Slater [Slater1950]_."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:68
msgid "Ti 3d–O 2pの混成の役割"
msgstr "Role of Ti 3d–O 2p Hybridization"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:70
msgid ""
"CohenとKrakauerは、立方晶BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ "
"のLAPW法の全エネルギー計算で、TiとOが大きく混成し、Baはほぼイオン的なBa\\ :sup:`2+`\\ "
"としてふるまうことを示し、Ti–Oの混成が強誘電不安定性に欠かせないと結論した "
"[CohenKrakauer1990]_。Cohenはさらに、閉殻の球対称なイオンを仮定して混成を含まないイオン模型（potential-"
"induced breathing模型）では、 "
"長距離のクーロン相互作用が極性の変位を好んでも短距離の反発が勝ち、立方晶が安定になることを示した。LAPW計算でTi 3dの寄与を抑えると、 "
"不安定性は消える。Ti 3d–O 2pの混成が短距離の反発を弱め、:eq:`fo-kappa-split` の "
":math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm{SR}}` を小さくすることで、 不安定性を可能にしている [PdosCohen1992]_。"
msgstr ""
"Using LAPW total-energy calculations for cubic BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , Cohen"
" and Krakauer found strong Ti–O hybridization and showed that Ba behaves "
"almost like ionic Ba\\ :sup:`2+`\\ . They concluded that Ti–O "
"hybridization is essential for the ferroelectric instability "
"[CohenKrakauer1990]_. Cohen further showed that in an ionic model "
"assuming closed-shell, spherically symmetric ions and excluding "
"hybridization (the potential-induced breathing model), long-range Coulomb"
" interactions favor polar displacements, but short-range repulsion wins "
"and the cubic structure is stable. Suppressing the Ti 3d contribution in "
"the LAPW calculation removes the instability. Ti 3d–O 2p hybridization "
"weakens short-range repulsion and enables the instability by reducing the"
" term in Equation :eq:`fo-kappa-split` denoted by "
":math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm{SR}}` [PdosCohen1992]_."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:76
msgid ""
"混成の存在は、\\ :ref:`射影状態密度<projected-dos>`\\ にも表れる。主にO 2pからなる価電子帯にTi "
"3dの重みが現れることは、 占有状態がO 2pとTi 3dの混じった状態であることを示す（\\ :ref:`orbital-"
"hybridization`\\ の2準位模型）。ただし、PDOSの重みは "
"混成の行列要素そのものではなく、混成が不安定性の原因であることまでは示さない。原因であることの根拠は、上の計算のように "
"混成を取り除くと不安定性が消えることにある。 `計算事例「二重井戸ポテンシャル Part 2」 <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/total-energy.html#ti-3d>`_\\ も、Ti "
"3dを除く試験は行っておらず、因果の根拠を文献に置いている。"
msgstr ""
"Hybridization also shows up in the \\ :ref:`projected density of states "
"<projected-dos>` \\ (PDOS). Ti 3d weight in the predominantly O 2p "
"valence bands shows that the occupied states mix O 2p and Ti 3d (see \\ "
":ref:`Orbital Hybridization and Spectral Overlap <orbital-hybridization>`"
" \\ for the two-level model). However, the PDOS weights are not the "
"hybridization matrix elements themselves and do not establish that "
"hybridization causes the instability. The evidence for causation is that "
"the instability disappears when hybridization is removed, as in the "
"calculations above. The `calculation example “Double-Well Potential, Part"
" 2” <https://example.quloud-platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/total-energy.html"
"#ti-3d>`_ \\  likewise does not test the removal of Ti 3d and relies on "
"the literature for evidence of causation."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:82
msgid ""
"混成は、Born有効電荷を通じてクーロン相互作用の側にも効く。Ghosezらは、Tiの大きなBorn有効電荷の主な部分がO "
"2pのバンドから生じ、Tiが動くとO 2pの\\ :ref:`Wannier関数の中心<fo-berry-phase>`\\ "
"が逆向きに動くことを示した。Ti–Oの距離が縮むとO 2pとTi 3dの混成が変わり、電子がOからTiへ移るためである "
"[GhosezMichenaudGonze1998]_。有効電荷が大きくなれば、:eq:`fo-dipole` の係数も大きくなる。"
msgstr ""
"Hybridization also affects the Coulomb interaction through the Born "
"effective charge. Ghosez and coauthors showed that the O 2p bands account"
" for most of the large Ti Born effective charge and that when Ti moves, "
"the \\ :ref:`Wannier function centers <fo-berry-phase>` \\ for O 2p move "
"in the opposite direction. This happens because decreasing the Ti–O "
"distance changes the O 2p and Ti 3d hybridization, transferring electrons"
" from O to Ti [GhosezMichenaudGonze1998]_. A larger effective charge also"
" increases the coefficient in Equation :eq:`fo-dipole`."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:85
msgid ""
"同じペロブスカイト型のPbTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ では、Pb–Oの混成も加わり、大きなひずみを伴って正方晶が安定になる。BaTiO\\ "
":sub:`3`\\ ではBa–Oの結合が ほぼイオン的で、菱面体晶が最も安定になる "
"[PdosCohen1992]_。Aサイトの原子の結合の性質が、どの相が低温で現れるかを左右する。"
msgstr ""
"In the related perovskite PbTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , Pb–O hybridization also "
"contributes and the tetragonal phase is stabilized with a large strain. "
"In BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , Ba–O bonding is nearly ionic and the rhombohedral"
" phase is most stable [PdosCohen1992]_. The bonding of the A-site atom "
"influences which phase appears at low temperature."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:91
msgid "有限温度の相の順序と変位の相関"
msgstr "Phase Sequence and Displacement Correlations at Finite Temperature"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:93
msgid ""
"ZhongとVanderbilt、Rabeは、局所的なモードの自己エネルギー、:eq:`fo-dipole` "
"の双極子の相互作用、短距離の相互作用、 ひずみとの結合を第一原理計算で決めた有効ハミルトニアンを作り、モンテカルロ法で解いた "
"[Zhong1994]_ [Zhong1995]_。 "
"立方晶・正方晶・直方晶・菱面体晶の順に現れる相の順序は、実験と一致した。LDAの体積の過小評価を補う負の圧力（−4.8 GPa）を "
"かけた計算での転移温度は、立方晶–正方晶が297 K（論文に併記された実験値403 K）、正方晶–直方晶が230 K（278 K）、 "
"直方晶–菱面体晶が200 K（183 "
"K）で、上の二つの転移は実験より低い（同論文の表III、:math:`14\\times14\\times14` 胞の値）。"
msgstr ""
"Zhong, Vanderbilt, and Rabe constructed an effective Hamiltonian with "
"first-principles parameters for the local-mode self-energy, the dipole "
"interaction in Equation :eq:`fo-dipole`, short-range interactions, and "
"coupling to strain. They solved it by Monte Carlo simulation [Zhong1994]_"
" [Zhong1995]_. The phase sequence agreed with experiment: cubic, "
"tetragonal, orthorhombic, then rhombohedral. Applying a negative pressure"
" (−4.8 GPa) to compensate for the LDA underestimate of the volume gave "
"transition temperatures of 297 K for cubic to tetragonal (the "
"experimental value quoted in the paper is 403 K), 230 K for tetragonal to"
" orthorhombic (278 K), and 200 K for orthorhombic to rhombohedral (183 "
"K). The two higher-temperature transitions occur at lower temperatures in"
" the calculation than in the experiment (values for the "
":math:`14\\times14\\times14` cell in Table III of the paper)."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:99
msgid ""
"立方晶相の転移温度のすぐ上で、各胞の局所的な変位の分布は弱く二つの山をもち、不安定な揺らぎは "
"Γ点からX点への方向にゾーン境界まで広がっていた。彼らは立方晶–正方晶転移を、\\ :ref:`変位型と秩序–無秩序型<displacive-"
"order-disorder>`\\ の 中間で、やや秩序–無秩序型に近いと結論した "
"[Zhong1995]_。揺らぎがΓ点からXの方向に広がることは、上で導いた鎖状の相関の表れで、 立方晶の\\ :ref:`フォノン分散"
"<phonon-batio3-example>`\\ で不安定な分枝がXとMの方向へ平らに広がることとも整合する。 "
"X線の散漫散乱、二体分布関数（PDF）、X線吸収微細構造（XAFS）で調べた局所的なTiの変位と平均構造の違いは、 「\\ "
":ref:`ferroelectricity`\\ 」の\\ :ref:`事例<fe-local-average>`\\ で扱う。"
msgstr ""
"Just above the transition temperature of the cubic phase, the "
"distribution of local displacements in the cells was weakly bimodal, and "
"unstable fluctuations extended from the Γ point toward X as far as the "
"zone boundary. The authors concluded that the cubic-to-tetragonal "
"transition was intermediate between \\ :ref:`displacive and "
"order–disorder <displacive-order-disorder>`\\ , but somewhat closer to "
"order–disorder [Zhong1995]_. The spread of the fluctuations from the Γ "
"point toward X reflects the chain-like correlations derived above. It is "
"also consistent with the flat unstable branch extending toward X and M in"
" the cubic \\ :ref:`phonon dispersion <phonon-batio3-example>`\\ . For "
"the differences between local Ti displacements and the average structure "
"studied by diffuse X-ray scattering, pair distribution function (PDF) "
"analysis, and X-ray absorption fine structure (XAFS), see the \\ "
":ref:`Ferroelectricity and Crystal Structure <ferroelectricity>` \\ "
"article's \\ :ref:`worked example <fe-local-average>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:109
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:111
msgid ""
":eq:`fo-kappa-split` の分け方は一意ではなく、:math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm{SR}}` と "
":math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm C}` の値は分け方によって変わる。 物理的に意味があるのは和の :math:`\\kappa`"
" であり、分けた値は物質の比較や傾向の説明に使う。"
msgstr ""
"The decomposition in Equation :eq:`fo-kappa-split` is not unique: the "
"values of :math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm{SR}}` and :math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm C}`"
" depend on how the contributions are separated. Their sum, "
":math:`\\kappa`, is the physically meaningful quantity. The separate "
"values are used to compare materials and explain trends."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:114
msgid ""
"混成が不安定性の原因であるという結論は、混成を取り除いた計算との比較による。ある構造のPDOSに混成が見えることや、 "
"変位とともにPDOSが変わることは、この機構と整合するが、それだけでは因果を示さない。PDOSで山が重なることは、\\ :ref:`混成"
"<orbital-hybridization>`\\ の十分条件でもない。"
msgstr ""
"The conclusion that hybridization causes the instability comes from "
"comparison with calculations that remove hybridization. Hybridization "
"seen in the PDOS of a structure, and changes in the PDOS with "
"displacement, are consistent with this mechanism, but these observations "
"alone do not establish causation. Overlapping peaks in the PDOS are also "
"insufficient to establish \\ :ref:`hybridization <orbital-"
"hybridization>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectric_origin.rst:117
msgid ""
"有効ハミルトニアンの転移温度は、パラメータを決めた第一原理計算の近似（交換相関汎関数と、体積を補う圧力）に依存する。 "
"相の順序が実験と一致しても、転移温度に十数〜約100 Kの差が残ることは、この種の計算の精度の目安になる。"
msgstr ""
"Transition temperatures from the effective Hamiltonian depend on the "
"approximations used to determine its parameters in first-principles "
"calculations (the exchange-correlation functional and the pressure used "
"to compensate for the volume). Even when the phase sequence agrees with "
"experiment, differences from just over 10 K to about 100 K remain in the "
"transition temperatures. These differences give a rough indication of the"
" accuracy of this type of calculation."

